The first seven lessons squeezed into a few tables for a last look before an interview. In the complexities, n is the container's current size, and "amortized" means an occasional slow step that averages out to the stated cost.

## Sequence containers

| Container | Operation | Cost | One-liner |
|---|---|---|---|
| `vector` | append / remove at the back | amortized O(1) / O(1) | `a.push_back(x); a.pop_back();` |
| `vector` | index | O(1) | `a[i]`, or `a.at(i)` while debugging |
| `vector` | insert / erase in the middle | O(n) | `a.insert(a.begin() + i, x); a.erase(a.begin() + i);` |
| `vector` | 2D grid | O(nm) | `vector<vector<int>> g(n, vector<int>(m));` |
| `string` | append a character | amortized O(1) | `s += c;` |
| `string` | substring | O(len) | `s.substr(i, len)` (the second argument is a length) |
| `string` | search | O(nm) worst | `s.find(t) != string::npos` |
| `deque` | in and out at both ends | O(1) | `d.push_front(x); d.pop_back();` |
| `stack` | push / top / pop | O(1) | `st.push(x); st.top(); st.pop();` |
| `queue` | push / front / pop | O(1) | `q.push(x); q.front(); q.pop();` |

## Heaps, sorted containers, hash containers

| Container | Operation | Cost | One-liner |
|---|---|---|---|
| `priority_queue` | max-heap push / pop | O(log n) | `priority_queue<int> pq;` |
| `priority_queue` | min-heap | O(log n) | `priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> pq;` |
| `priority_queue` | build from a range | O(n) | `priority_queue<int> pq(a.begin(), a.end());` |
| `set` | insert / erase / lookup | O(log n) | `s.insert(x); s.erase(x); s.count(x);` |
| `set` | minimum / maximum | O(1) | `*s.begin(); *s.rbegin();` |
| `set` | first ≥ x / > x | O(log n) | `s.lower_bound(x); s.upper_bound(x);` |
| `multiset` | erase one x | O(log n) | `ms.erase(ms.find(x));` |
| `map` | count | O(log n) | `cnt[x]++;` |
| `map` | walk in key order | O(n) | `for (auto& [k, v] : m)` |
| `unordered_map` | count / lookup | O(1) average | `cnt[x]++; m.find(k) != m.end();` |
| `unordered_set` | spot a repeat | O(1) average | `if (!seen.insert(x).second) /* repeat */;` |

## Algorithms

| Operation | Cost | One-liner |
|---|---|---|
| sort / descending | O(n log n) | `sort(a.begin(), a.end()); sort(a.rbegin(), a.rend());` |
| stable sort | O(n log n) | `stable_sort(a.begin(), a.end(), cmp);` |
| index of the first ≥ x | O(log n) | `lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x) - a.begin()` |
| occurrences of x | O(log n) | `upper_bound(...) - lower_bound(...)` |
| dedupe after sorting | O(n) | `a.erase(unique(a.begin(), a.end()), a.end());` |
| maximum / minimum | O(n) | `*max_element(a.begin(), a.end())` |
| sum | O(n) | `accumulate(a.begin(), a.end(), 0LL)` |
| reverse | O(n) | `reverse(a.begin(), a.end());` |
| fill 0, 1, 2, … | O(n) | `iota(a.begin(), a.end(), 0);` |
| next permutation | O(n) | `next_permutation(a.begin(), a.end())` |

